I'll say it up front: aside from this being my first Priest ascension,
nothing terribly interesting here.

Sanae started all puny and squishy, with a mediocre statline and
spellbooks of clairvoyance and cure sickness; I was almost taken out
by a jackal around turn 500.  My cat Chen died pretty early, so I
leveled up a lot and was soon being chased around by soldier ants.
Fortunately, I managed to pick up a magic lamp in a random shop.
Blessed +2 GDSM, please.  Well, +0 to you too.

Anyway, after retaking Minetown from the soldier ants, I happened upon
another magic lamp in Izchak's.  Hmm, maybe I'll get myself a Staff of
Aesculapius, since I can't really use any other good artifact
weapons.

Tame djinni.  Great.

He did kill some shopkeepers before falling into Fort Ludios and
getting separated from me, though, so it wasn't all bad.  That aside,
the midgame was long and uneventful, with the elephant in the room
being the 13(!) levels gained from one incubus.  In front of my Quest
leader, no less.  Must be one of the more liberal sects.

I breached the Castle with spells of knock and wizard lock, in the
process giving some unfortunate trolls a severe headache (and
neckache, and bodyache,) quickly found the wand of wishing, and
finally got that Staff of Aesculapius.  I also picked up an Eye of the
Aethiopica to complement my 400+ Pw.  I then doubled back to my stash
to get the Staff up to +6, then back to the Quest to show Nalzok my
new toy.

There was one close call (aside from a dragon's lightning breath
blowing up my wand of death when I stormed Ludios without
reflection.)  While crossing the lake on the Medusa level, I
accidentally removed my ring of levitation instead of my blindfold.
Oops.  Thank Hermes there was a land square nearby; that could've been
a YASD for the ages.

All that aside, things were turning up Sanae.  I'd found a spellbook
of magic mapping earlier; with the spellbooks of magic missile and
identify I found in Gehennom, I mostly breezed through.  Except for
the liches.  I never did find a scroll of genocide (my one genocide
was from a throne.)  Those punks.  Anyway, I was able to find some
gauntlets of dexterity (albeit cursed -2, nothing a wand of
cancellation couldn't handle) and silver dragon scales to finish up my
ascension kit, so I could save my wishes.

I levelported into the Sanctum, finding myself outside the temple.  A
random demon summoned Yeenoghu, but I drove him off and got in--where
I found the high priest's corpse with no Amulet.  Having a pretty good
idea what had happened, I waited for Yeenoghu to come back, then
immediately used my cursed potion of gain level to go back up, then
came down again and stood on the up stairs while I beat the Amulet out
of Yeenoghu.

The mysterious force hit me moderately hard.  On the way up, I ran
into Juiblex and Asmodeus; I'd been wondering where those guys were on
my way down.  At any rate, they didn't give me too much trouble.

I stopped by Home on the way up to see what my Quest leader would
say.  Big mistake.  While I was passing through one of the temple's
hallways, a bunch of monsters appeared on either side of me, and the
two adjacent were arch-liches.  I put on my ring of teleport control
and began to take out a scroll of teleportation before remembering
that the level was no-teleport (you'd think I'd have known that after
spending 5000 turns there with an incubus.)

That little unpleasantry aside, the Planes went smoothly.  I avoided
doing anything grossly stupid, and I wore my oilskin cloak for Water.
On Astral, I was walking on eggshells because my last character had
died to Pestilence there.  Fortunately, the first altar I tried, the
one guarded by Famine, was the Neutral one.  Yay!

